# Data Dawg — athlete answers are conversation

Data Dawg answers about a specific athlete (search, "who is…", "tell me about…") are **written by
the model from verified facts**. They are not a rendered template. `get_athlete_full_dossier`
returns `facts`; `buildAthleteFacts` in `lib/data-dawg-athlete-dossier.ts` builds them.

## The shape of an answer

1. **Two or three short paragraphs of prose.** No section headings, no labelled fields, no emoji,
   no arrows, no bullet lists unless the user asked for a list.
2. **Never these section labels:** `Career snapshot:`, `Development path:`, `Career progression:`,
   `Detailed results:`, `Historical context:`, `National résumé:`, `Notable achievements:`, or a
   source / verification / confidence footer. They were removed on purpose — the printout voice is
   what this replaced. Do not reintroduce them anywhere in the answer path.
3. **Never walk the record year by year unless the user asks.** Compress to an arc: "back-to-back
   4A titles as a junior and senior" beats four dated lines. The year-by-year list is correct only
   as a reply to "year by year", "his NHSCA results", "show me all of it".
4. **Close with one short offer** of what else we hold — and only when there is more.

## Links

- **The first mention of the name is the profile hyperlink**, once, in the opening sentence.
- Use `getAthleteProfileUrl(id)` → `https://app.ncwrestlingunited.com/view-profile?id=…`
  (not `/unified-profile/[id]`, not `/athletes/[id]`). Open same-tab in chat HTML.
- **No `profile_url` means no link.** Alumni who predate the athlete directory get a plain-text
  name. Never emit a link with a placeholder, ellipsis, or guessed id.
- **Never link a name to an image.** Any tool that returns athlete rows to the model must map them
  through `getAthleteProfileUrl(id)` and strip `photourl` / `photo_url` / `headshot_url` first —
  otherwise the model uses the only URL it was given and links names to headshot PNGs.

## Facts, not adjectives

- Every number, placement, school and year must come from a tool result or supplied facts. An
  empty array means we hold nothing on record — not zero, not "never competed".
- **Decide it in code, not in the prompt.** Tense (`career_complete`), the college line
  (`college_path`), and whether a prospect rank is publishable are computed in `buildAthleteFacts`
  and passed as `writing_notes`. A rule buried in the system prompt loses to a directive sitting
  next to the data. Add new ones the same way.
- Weight belongs on tournament result lines only — never a header field; it changes constantly.
- Transfers read chronologically, original school first: `UNC Chapel Hill → NC State`. A transfer
  is never described as a fresh commitment.
- Four straight titles are **four consecutive** / every high school season — never "back-to-back".
- Never infer a Fargo "Blood Round" from a W–L unless the round is explicitly stored.
